    {
      "annotation_id": "44759c9b17dd4eb5bae6a40a5603a883_98",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is argued that the PFA Act has been recently amended which prescribes the punishment of fine also."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "37f4ef745d854922a6704a5aa9e548e4_99",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is prayed that in view of pendency of case for a long period, a lenient view may kindly be taken."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c06f78291ee54f3e86be479845232bd9_100",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On the other hand it is argued on behalf of department by Ld."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fbc768a0094146f2a89ea1ada38fbdd5_103",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Trial Court has already taken a lenient view and there is no illegality in the order of sentence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f5fe497c2cfa4c058f500ef161cde16a_104",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "15. The appellant/convict is convicted for commission of offence punishable under Section 16(1)(a) of PFA Act wherein the minimum sentence of imprisonment was awarded."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "04d01dab8b274d40afdab57978c5662a_106",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "16. In view of above, question for consideration before this court is whether after repeal of earlier Act and introduction of new Act which contains the lesser punishment, the court can take a lenient view of awarding the lesser punishment."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "70d851a8b9f14af99ec291410c2ea93d_107",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On this issue, Hon'ble Supreme Court in case titled as M/s A. K. Sarkar & Company &\nAnr. Vs. The State of West Bengal & Ors, Special Leave Petition(Criminal) No.6095 of 2018, dated 07.03.2024, has observed that:\n\"Whether the appellant can b"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "187de0eb146f4d0ea9379e61bd763437_108",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This court in T. Barai VS. Henry Ah Hoe (1983) 1 SCC 177, had held that when an amendment is beneficial to the accused it can be applied even to cases pending the courts where such Digitally signed by Kiran Kiran Gupta Date:\nGupta 2024.05.3"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6822287be7644bbf959bbae9f51e894c_109",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n17. The recent judgment of Hon'ble Supreme Court in case M/s A. K. Sarkar & Company &\nAnr.(supra) has made it clear that if there is an amendment in the Act, which is beneficial to the accused, it can be applied even to the pending cases i"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "19f57e7ce86641a480105fb4eaa53879_110",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The ratio of judgment M/s A. K. Sarkar & Company & Anr.(supra) is squarely applicable to the facts of present case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "29fa8ef74d3f47438d28817cb6c58f3b_111",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore on the basis of above case law, I have no hesitation to hold that this court can take a lenient view as per new provisions of law."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7e25aeab9559436c9a6879c3ce258076_112",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "18. In the present case the complaint was filed on 15.05.2006."
